# Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded inverse hyperbolic sine of B32
#
# Small |x| goes through an odd polynomial in B64. Otherwise
# asinh(|x|) = log(|x| + sqrt(x^2 + 1)), with the logarithm reduced through a
# 128-entry reciprocal table and a short polynomial. A longer polynomial
# settles the cases the first can't round. Round to nearest only: ±0 and ±inf
# map to themselves, NaN comes back quiet.
#
# Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary32/asinh/asinhf.c via RazorForge's B32Asinh.rf.
# Copyright (c) 2023 Alexei Sibidanov <sibid@uvic.ca>
# MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard/Core

